    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Anu wrote 3 + 4 x 2. Ravi wrote (3 + 4) x 2. They got different answers.\n\"Brackets matter,\" said the teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "bracket",
     "order",
     "simplify"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Do brackets first, then multiplication and division from left to right, then addition and subtraction from left to right. 3 + 4 x 2 is 3 + 8, which is 11.\nWith brackets, (3 + 4) x 2 is 7 x 2, which is 14.\nBrackets can change the answer, so we use them to show what to do first."
    }
   },
